.git
.github
.claude
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.venv
venv
env

# Local store / generated artifacts -- never belong in a server image
memory/
benchmark/
tests/
assets/

# The client package stays out of the server image -- with named exceptions,
# one per module hub/ actually imports. Both exist for the same reason: the
# Hub and the client must produce the SAME numbers, and a near-copy that
# drifted would not fail loudly, it would return confident and wrong ones.
#
#   overlap.py     hub/commons.py -- MinHash. Signatures are only comparable
#                  if both sides draw the same permutations.
#   experiment.py  hub/outcomes.py -- the outcome statistics. A drifted copy
#                  would make the customer's own `commontrace experiment` and
#                  the operator's `hub.manage outcomes` disagree about the
#                  same fleet, which finishes the number as evidence.
#   retrieval.py   hub/bench_retrieval.py -- the LOCAL retrieval tier, used
#   _lexical.py    as the reference the Hub's own recall is reported against.
#                  Same reason again, in its sharpest form: that comparison
#                  is the entire finding (0.0% vs 84.8% recall@1 on identical
#                  records), and a reimplemented reference would be measuring
#                  the Hub against something no customer runs.
#                  _lexical.py is retrieval.py's own import, not a separate
#                  decision.
#
# All four are pure stdlib, so they add source to the image and no dependency.
#
# KEEP THIS LIST IN SYNC WITH THE IMPORTS. A module missing here does not
# break the build -- it breaks container START, with an ImportError on code
# that imports fine in every test run and every editable install. That is
# invisible until a deployment tries to boot, so
# hub/tests/test_image_contents.py asserts the two lists match and runs in
# every CI job, not only the Docker ones.
#
# Excluding the contents rather than the directory itself, so the negations
# below can re-include specific files (an excluded *directory* is never
# traversed, so `!commontrace/x.py` under a bare `commontrace/` rule would
# not match).
commontrace/**
!commontrace/__init__.py
!commontrace/overlap.py
!commontrace/experiment.py
# The validity audit that runs in front of every causal number
# (hub/crud.py:causal_effects). Without it the Hub answers
# fleet_outcomes with effect sizes and no way to tell whether the
# sample can support them -- and the container would not even start,
# because crud.py imports it at module level.
!commontrace/integrity.py
# Kaplan-Meier and the log-rank test, which integrity.py imports at module
# level to tell an occasion nobody has reported YET from one nobody ever
# will. Without it the container starts and dies on the import, and with the
# import stubbed the attrition audit would go back to reading a fast-
# concluding treated arm as missing data.
!commontrace/survival.py
# Content identity for a trace, stamped onto every holdout assignment
# (hub/crud.py:holdout_assign) so an amended trace cannot silently split
# an experiment's arms across two treatments. Imported at module level,
# so without it the container starts and dies.
!commontrace/revision.py
# Turns a causal effect into a quantity a price can attach to
# (hub/crud.py:value_delivered) -- the pricing basis STRATEGY.md 11.5
# names. Imported at module level, so without it the container starts
# and dies.
!commontrace/value.py
# Evidence decay: how old a measured effect may be and still be billed
# on. Imported by hub/crud.py at module scope (it also owns the horizon
# constant the working-set block reads). Pure stdlib.
!commontrace/decay.py
!commontrace/retrieval.py
!commontrace/_lexical.py
# retrieval.py's own import: the Porter stemmer behind the opt-in idf-v3
# scorer. Pure stdlib (functools).
!commontrace/_stem.py
# Secret/PII/prompt-injection screening (OWASP ASI06), imported at module
# level by hub/abuse.py:suspicion_reason so the same content-safety scan
# a customer's own `commontrace lesson approve` runs also gates
# contribute_trace/amend_trace on the Hub -- one implementation, not a
# copy that could drift and cover different patterns on each side. Pure
# stdlib (re, dataclasses). Imported at module level, so without it the
# container starts and dies.
!commontrace/memory_guard.py
# What an experiment committed to measuring before it could see the answer,
# and the diff of the run against it (hub/crud.py:causal_effects, and
# hub/manage.py:start_experiment, which writes the registration). Imported
# at module level, so without it the container starts and dies. Pure stdlib
# (datetime, hashlib, json, dataclasses).
!commontrace/prereg.py
# The assignment rows a customer re-runs the arithmetic from, and the digest
# the value ledger's signature commits to (hub/crud.py, hub/manage.py:
# export_assignments). Imported at module level. Pure stdlib (csv, hashlib,
# io, dataclasses).
!commontrace/raw_export.py
# Near-duplicate clustering (hub/crud.py:_cluster_representatives, used by
# holdout_for_results) -- the same reason as retrieval.py/_lexical.py
# above: a customer's own `commontrace distill` and the Hub's holdout
# randomization must treat "these are probably the same lesson" identically,
# or a trace the client would cluster locally fragments into its own
# randomization unit on the Hub instead. Imported at module level, so
# without it the container starts and dies. Pure stdlib (re, dataclasses,
# collections.Counter) plus its own two imports below.
!commontrace/distill.py
# distill.py's own import (STARTER_DOMAINS) -- pure stdlib (os, re, sys).
!commontrace/paths.py
# The harm policy's constants and `split` (hub/crud.py:search_traces and
# hub/manage.py:harm_policy), shared with the local tier so both decide the
# same way. Imported at module level, so without it the container starts
# and dies. Pure: imports only experiment.py. Reading the LOCAL store's
# evidence lives in commontrace/evidence.py, which the Hub never imports.
!commontrace/harm.py

# Secrets must come from the platform's secret store, never be baked in
.env
hub/.env
*.env
!hub/.env.example
